# ============================================================================
# setup/link.conf.local.example
#
# Copy to setup/link.conf.local (gitignored) to override link.conf on this
# host only. link.conf already holds the settings both ends share, including
# the field power values -- what belongs here is only what differs between
# the two machines, or between bench and field.
#
# Overriding WIFI_CHANNEL, BANDWIDTH, MCS_INDEX, STBC, LDPC, SHORT_GI,
# LINK_DOMAIN or WIFI_REGION here kills the link unless the peer matches:
# install.sh warns about it and prints a fingerprint of those values to
# compare between the hosts.
#
# After editing:
#   sudo ./install.sh --role air|gs --only 50-config
#   sudo systemctl restart wifibroadcast@drone   # or wifibroadcast@gs
# ============================================================================

# --- Bench work (either host) ------------------------------------------------
# Caps power for a module bus-powered from a Pi USB port. Both lines are
# needed: at usb-pi the ceiling is TXPOWER_MAX_USB=800, and a higher
# WIFI_TXPOWER inherited from link.conf aborts install.sh rather than being
# reduced to fit. Delete this file to return to link.conf's field values.
# POWER_SOURCE=usb-pi
# WIFI_TXPOWER=500

# --- Ground station ----------------------------------------------------------
# QGroundControl running on another machine on the LAN instead of on this Pi.
# Add a UDP connection in QGC pointing at this Pi's LAN address, port 14550.
# QGC_HOST=192.168.1.50

# --- Air ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The camera's own RTSP URL. Required on this host when VIDEO_ENABLE=1.
# The camera and this Pi's eth0 need static addresses in the same subnet,
# set outside this file -- see docs/integration.md.
# VIDEO_CAM_URL=rtsp://192.168.10.50:554/stream1
